The '''Zuzabol'''<ref name="DI3.0">''[[Disney Infinity 3.0]]''</ref> were a [[Sentience|sentient]] bipedal [[species]] shorter in height than [[human]]s.<ref name="TFA" /> The Zuzabol [[Avga Rosene]] and another member of the species worked as a [[fuel]]ing crew<ref name="Naming tweet">{{Twitter|pablohidalgo|status/697526913271783424|[[Pablo Hidalgo]]|quote=@IndianaJedi Name: Avga Rosene. Species: Zuzabol. That's about it.|archivefile=File:Avga Rosene tweets Pablo Hidalgo.png}}</ref> for the [[Resistance]]<ref name="TFA" /> in the [[Standard year|year]] [[34 ABY]].<ref name="Galactic Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> Both were present in the [[Resistance base]] on the [[planet]] [[D'Qar]] shortly before the [[Battle of Starkiller Base]].<ref name="TFA" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Zuzabol species first appeared in the film [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']],<ref name="TFA" /> which was released on [[December 16]], [[2015]].<ref name="Year by Year">''[[Star Wars Year By Year: A Visual History, Updated and Expanded Edition]]''</ref> The species were not identified in the film, but received a name in the non-[[canon]] [[Star Wars video games|video game]] ''[[Disney Infinity 3.0]]'', which was released in conjunction with the film.<ref name="DI3.0" /> Despite the game being non-[[canon]], story group member [[Pablo Hidalgo]] confirmed on [[Wikipedia:Twitter|Twitter]] that the names provided by the game for previously unidentified entities, including the Zuzabol, were considered canon.<ref name="Twitter">{{Twitter|pablohidalgo|status/749616406245699584|[[Pablo Hidalgo]]|date=2016-07-03|quote=@LelalMekha Yeah, same with Infinity.|archivefile=File:PabloHidalgo-LegoName-Twitter.png|nolive=1}} {{C|In response to: "@pablohidalgo <nowiki>youtube.com/watch?v=JwxAeHPLpPg</nowiki> The Lego game identifies a few BG characters from TFA, but are those names canonical?"}}</ref>

